35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the ledger shows seventy percent of costs are fixed, regardless of attendance. The sign-up records reveal eleven mid-year joiners, each requiring manual calculation. This administrative burden is unsustainable.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the ledger is a map, not the territory. My hours show chasing individual payments takes six hours monthly, versus one for yearly. We must stop the administrative bleed.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shunichi, the data is stark. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work, and eighteen never show. The same nine handle setup. Is the fee truly fair?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the numbers are cold, but the silence is loud. Turnout dropped a third after the door charge. People stopped feeling like they belonged.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, six hours chasing payments is a disaster! The bank statements show a third needed reminders. We need a system that doesn’t rely on nagging people.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the door charge is a barrier. If the fee feels like a toll, newcomers drift away. We need a structure that preserves anonymity and ease of entry, not one that polices attendance.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, precisely. The data confirms the rot. We must shift to a model that minimizes the administrative burden, or we lose the next treasurer entirely.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I agree. But if the same nine carry the load, a flat fee feels like a tax on the absent. We need to see if the work justifies the cost.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, the rot is social, not financial. If the fee feels like a toll, people stop showing up. We need to fix the belonging, not just the books.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, belonging is great, but you can’t pay for it with empty promises! I need hard numbers to stop the guessing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, the ledger proves costs are fixed, not variable. A flat fee is the only logical structure. It preserves the anonymity that keeps newcomers comfortable, without penalizing those who attend less.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, the ledger proves the administrative cost is the variable, not the attendance. A flat fee eliminates the six-hour monthly chase. I support Asuka’s logic.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
